    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33384" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paetus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a surname.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Q. Aelius Paetus, <i>consul with</i> M. Junius Pennus, A. U. C.
			587.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> P.
			Aelius Paetus, <i>an augur</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
			36</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			L. Papirius Paetus, <i>a friend of Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				1, 20, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 1, 12</span></i>. To him are addressed the
			letters of Cicero, ad Fam. 9, 15-26.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
